{"id":"aa2378ce-3342-4fe0-8a80-f7d2ddebdd11","object":"chat.completion","created":1789996843,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"schema\":\"amr-supervisor/v1\",\"select\":[{\"when\":\"OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB\",\"action\":\"SelectA\"},{\"when\":\"OwnerFree and RequestB and not RequestA\",\"action\":\"SelectB\"},{\"when\":\"OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB\",\"action\":\"SelectA\"},{\"when\":\"True\",\"action\":\"Defer\"}],\"step\":[{\"when\":\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"Stopped\"},{\"when\":\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\",\"action\":\"Finish\",\"next\":\"Done\"},{\"when\":\"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\",\"action\":\"Release\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"},{\"when\":\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\",\"action\":\"Brake\",\"next\":\"BrakeRequested\"},{\"when\":\"not OwnReservation and not Released\",\"action\":\"Request\",\"next\":\"Waiting\"},{\"when\":\"ModeStopped\",\"action\":\"Resume\",\"next\":\"ResumePending\"},{\"when\":\"True\",\"action\":\"Proceed\",\"next\":\"Traversing\"}]}","reasoning_content":"We need answer only JSON. Need synthesize restricted supervisory program. Need obey all constraints. Need final exactly JSON object no markdown. Need design select and step rules <=12 each, total branches <=32? Need interpret branches maybe number rules? at most 32 total branches. We can do select maybe 4 rules, step maybe 7 rules. Need ensure totality for select: all 32 boolean combos result. Step: all 7 modes * 256 facts result. Need expressions only Boolean names, True/False, not/and/or/paren, precedence. Need conditions <=512 chars, <=64 AST nodes, depth <=8. Need rule first true. select cannot use step/mode. Step cannot use select names. Actions exact strings. next explicit mode string for step. Need duplicate keys no.\n\nNeed carefully map policy.\n\nWe need produce JSON with schema, select array, step array.\n\nWe need design select rules for inputs OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, PreferA, PreferB. Actions SelectA, SelectB, Defer. Requirements:\n- Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA.\n- Selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB.\n- If reservation free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer.\n- Otherwise Defer required.\n- When both eligible, either legal; preferences advisory no obligation, may conflict/absent.\n\nNeed rule set total for all 32 combos. Since preferences not mandatory, can ignore PreferA/B? But select inputs include them; expressions may not mention. Need every possible input result. We can do:\n1. when OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB -> SelectA\n2. when OwnerFree and RequestB and not RequestA -> SelectB\n3. when OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB -> SelectA (or preference maybe either)\n4. when True -> Defer\nThis handles free & at least one request. But if RequestA true RequestB true, rule1? if RequestB true, false. rule2 false. rule3 true. Good. If only RequestA: rule1 true. Only RequestB: rule2 true. No requests: rule4 Defer. OwnerFree false: rule4. Preferences ignored. At most 4. Could use preferences? Not necessary. Need ensure select cannot use step names. Good.\n\nStep rules evaluate first applicable requirement. Need parse P1 exactly.\n\nInputs:\nObservationUsable, PedestrianBlocked, OwnReservation, Released, BodyClearOfZ, Halted, AtGoal, TaskActive. Mode flags ModeIdle, ModeWaiting, ModeTraversing, ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped, ModeResumePending, ModeDone. Exactly one mode flag true. Need rules first applicable policy. Later req never override earlier irrespective mode.\n\nPolicy:\n1. An unusable observation, inactive task, or blocked pedestrian crossing requires Brake. If Halted true, next Stopped; else BrakeRequested.\nBlocking conditions absent = ObservationUsable AND TaskActive AND not PedestrianBlocked? Since \"unusable observation, inactive task, or blocked pedestrian crossing\" means blocking if not ObservationUsable OR not TaskActive OR PedestrianBlocked. So req1 applies if (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked. Action Brake. next Stopped if Halted else BrakeRequested. Need two rules:\n1a when (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted -> Brake, next Stopped.\n1b when (not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted -> Brake, next BrakeRequested.\nOrder? If Halted true use first. Need if Halted false second. Could combine? Step rule action and next cannot be conditional. Need separate. First applicable. If we put Halted true first, then false rule. If blocking absent, skip.\n\n2. With those blocking conditions absent, a robot that is AtGoal and has Released must establish stop confirmation before reporting completion: if not Halted, return Brake with next mode BrakeRequested; if Halted, return Finish with next mode Done.\nNeed blocking absent: ObservationUsable and TaskActive and not PedestrianBlocked. AtGoal and Released.\n2a if AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish next Done.\n2b if AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake next BrakeRequested.\nOrder? Both after req1. Halted true first then false. Need if req1 false. Good.\n\n3. If neither previous applies and OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ are true, return Release with next Traversing. This takes priority even if current mode BrakeRequested.\nSo condition: no req1, no req2, and OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ. Need encode \"neither previous applies\" as blocking absent AND not(AtGoal and Released). Since if req2 applies when AtGoal & Released & blocking absent. But if blocking absent not needed? Policy says if neither previous applies and OwnReservation/BodyClear. Since req1 applies under blocking; req2 under blocking absent + AtGoal&Released. So condition for req3: not blocking AND not(AtGoal and Released) AND OwnReservation AND BodyClearOfZ. But wait if blocking false? \"neither previous applies\" includes req1 not apply. If req1 applies, cannot do Release. So yes. Could simply after req1/req2 rules, write when OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release. Because first applicable order ensures req1/req2 checked before, so if we place after them, condition need not include negations. But for independent evaluation, first applicable. If req1 false and req2 false, then this true if OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ. That's correct. If req1 true, earlier catches. If req2 true, earlier catches. So rule 3 can be `\"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\", action Release next Traversing`. But need consider if blocking conditions absent? If req1 false implies blocking absent. Yes because req1 condition is blocking. So okay. If req1 false and req2 false, then if OwnReservation & BodyClearOfZ release. Policy 3 says if neither previous applies and OwnReservation/BodyClear. Yes.\n\nHowever, there is subtlety: req2 condition requires blocking absent. If blocking present and AtGoal/Released, req1 catches. If blocking absent and AtGoal/Released, req2 catches. If blocking present and OwnReservation/BodyClear, req1 catches. Good.\n\n4. Otherwise, a robot in BrakeRequested with Halted false must keep Brake and next BrakeRequested.\nCondition after previous. Current mode ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. Action Brake, next BrakeRequested.\nNeed \"Otherwise\" means if no earlier. Since earlier rules catch some; but if we place after, condition only ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. However if earlier requirement applies? It will be caught earlier. If previous not apply and mode BrakeRequested and Halted false, do this. If Halted true? Policy says with Halted false. If Halted true and BrakeRequested and not blocked etc and not OwnReservation/BodyClear? Then skip to later. Later? Requirement 5 etc. Need follow.\nRule 4 when ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake next BrakeRequested.\n\n5. Otherwise, if both OwnReservation and Released are false, return Request with next Waiting.\nCondition after prev: not OwnReservation and not Released. Action Request next Waiting.\nNeed consider if earlier applies. If e.g. blocking, req1. If AtGoal Released etc. If OwnReservation BodyClear, req3. If mode BrakeRequested & not Halted, req4. So rule after.\n\n6. Otherwise, if current mode is Stopped, return Resume with next ResumePending.\nCondition after prev: ModeStopped. Action Resume next ResumePending.\n\n7. In every remaining case return Proceed with next Traversing.\nCondition True. Action Proceed next Traversing.\n\nNeed ensure step rules <=12. Let's count:\n1 blocking+Halted -> Brake/Stopped\n2 blocking+not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested\n3 AtGoal&Released&Halted & blocking absent? If we omit blocking absent, then if blocking present and Halted, rule1 catches. If blocking present and not Halted, rule2 catches. So rule3 after those can just be AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish/Done. But wait if blocking present and Halted true, rule1 catches first. If blocking absent and Halted true and AtGoal Released, rule3 true. Good. If blocking present and Halted false, rule2 catches. So no need blocking absent.\n4 AtGoal&Released&not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested. But if blocking present and not Halted, rule2 catches. If blocking absent, rule4. Good. Need order after blocking. If Halted false and AtGoal/Released, yes.\n5 OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release/Traversing. If earlier not apply. If AtGoal Released not relevant. If blocking present, rule1/2. If AtGoal Released, rule3/4. Good.\n6 ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested.\n7 not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request/Waiting.\n8 ModeStopped -> Resume/ResumePending.\n9 True -> Proceed/Traversing.\nTotal 9 step rules. select 4. Total 13 branches if branch=rule, <=32. Per function <=12. Good.\n\nNeed verify policy priority with this ordering. But we must be extremely careful: The step expressions may refer to mode flags. The mode flags are one-hot. We can refer to ModeBrakeRequested, ModeStopped. Need no select names.\n\nPotential issue: For step req3: \"If neither previous applies and OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ are true, return Release with next mode Traversing.\" It says \"This takes priority even if current mode is BrakeRequested.\" Our rule 5 after req1/2, before req4 (BrakeRequested) so yes. However, our rule 3/4 for AtGoal Released are before Release. Policy req2 before req3. Correct. But need consider if AtGoal and Released true but Halted false: req2 says Brake BrakeRequested. Our rule4 catches before Release. Correct.\n\nPotential issue: For req2, \"With those blocking conditions absent, a robot that is AtGoal and has Released must establish stop confirmation before reporting completion: if not Halted, return Brake with next mode BrakeRequested; if Halted, return Finish with next mode Done.\" Our rules 3/4 do not explicitly require blocking absent, but blocking present caught earlier. If blocking present and Halted true, rule1 catches Brake/Stopped not Finish. Good. If blocking present and Halted false, rule2 catches Brake/BrakeRequested. Same action and next as req2 for not Halted, but req1 priority; if Halted true conflict: req1 says Brake/Stopped, req2 says Finish/Done. Our rule1 catches. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Requirement 1 \"An unusable observation, an inactive task, or a blocked pedestrian crossing requires Brake. If Halted is true, next mode must be Stopped; otherwise BrakeRequested.\" If blocking and Halted true, Brake/Stopped. Our rule1. If blocking and Halted false, Brake/BrakeRequested. Our rule2. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Requirement 4 \"Otherwise, a robot in BrakeRequested with Halted false must keep Brake and next mode BrakeRequested.\" What if ModeBrakeRequested, Halted false, and OwnReservation/BodyClear? Req3 applies first, Release/Traversing. Our rule5 before rule6. Good. What if AtGoal Released Halted false? Req2 applies first Brake/BrakeRequested. Our rule4 before rule5? Actually rule4 AtGoal Released not Halted before rule5. It returns Brake/BrakeRequested, same as req4 but req2 priority. Good. What if blocking present? req1 catches. Good.\nWhat if ModeBrakeRequested Halted false and not OwnReservation and not Released? Req4 applies before req5, so Brake/BrakeRequested. Our rule6 before rule7. Good.\nWhat if ModeBrakeRequested Halted false and OwnReservation true but BodyClear false and Released maybe? Req3 false (BodyClear false). Req4 true. Our rule6. Good.\n\nRequirement 5 \"Otherwise, if both OwnReservation and Released are false, return Request with next Waiting.\" Need if ModeStopped and both false? Req5 before req6, so Request/Waiting, not Resume. Our rule7 before rule8. Good.\nRequirement 6 \"Otherwise, if current mode Stopped, return Resume with next ResumePending.\" If not both OwnReservation/Released false. Our rule8 after rule7. Good.\nRequirement 7 remaining Proceed.\n\nNeed ensure every possible input result. Step rules with final True. Good.\n\nNow, need consider constraints on expressions: \"Expressions allow only True, False, the permitted Boolean names, not, and, or, and parentheses, with Python Boolean precedence. No calls, comparisons, arithmetic, attributes, new names, or assignment. A condition has at most 512 characters, 64 Python syntax-tree nodes and expression depth eight.\"\n\nWe need write expressions valid. Use `not` lower-case, `and`, `or`, parentheses. Python precedence: `not` > `and` > `or`. Our expressions can include not with parentheses. Need ensure no extra syntax like `!`. JSON string.\n\nSelect expressions:\nRule1: \"OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB\"\nRule2: \"OwnerFree and RequestB and not RequestA\"\nRule3: \"OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB\"\nRule4: \"True\"\nAlternatively could simplify rule1: OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB. If both requests and PreferB, selects A. Legal either. Good.\nBut wait if OwnerFree true, RequestA true, RequestB false, rule1 SelectA. If OwnerFree true, RequestA false, RequestB true, rule2 SelectB. If both true, rule3 SelectA. If OwnerFree true, RequestA true, RequestB true but rule1 false because not RequestB false. rule2 false. rule3 true. Good.\nIf OwnerFree true, RequestA false, RequestB false, rule4 Defer.\nIf OwnerFree false but requests true, rule1/2/3 all include OwnerFree false, rule4 Defer.\nPreferences ignored. All input combos covered.\n\nPotential issue: \"If a reservation is free and at least one request exists, select an eligible robot, rather than Defer.\" Eligible means requires OwnerFree and Request. Our rules do. Good.\n\nStep expressions:\nNeed maybe include blocking condition exactly. Let's define B = `(not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked`. Expression string: \"(not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked\". Need parentheses? Python precedence: not > or. `not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked` is valid. But for clarity and AST depth. Use parentheses maybe. Condition length small. AST nodes maybe: Or, Or, Not, Name, Not, Name, Name = 7. Depth 3. Fine.\nRule1: `\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\"`\nNeed Python precedence: `and` lower than `or`? Actually Python precedence: `not` highest, `and` next, `or` lowest? Wait Python: `not` > `and` > `or`. So `(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted` with parentheses around or. If no parentheses, `not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked and Halted` would parse wrong. We include parentheses.\nRule2: `\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\"`\nRule3: `\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\"` (after blocking). But wait if blocking present and Halted true, rule1 catches. If blocking absent and Halted true, rule3. Good. But what if AtGoal and Released and Halted true but ObservationUsable false? Rule1 catches. Good.\nRule4: `\"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\"` (after rule3). If blocking present and not Halted, rule2 catches. If blocking absent, rule4. Good. But what if AtGoal Released Halted false and blocking absent? req2 says Brake/BrakeRequested. Our rule4. Good.\nRule5: `\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\"`\nRule6: `\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\"`\nRule7: `\"not OwnReservation and not Released\"`\nRule8: `\"ModeStopped\"`\nRule9: `\"True\"`\n\nNeed verify step priority for combinations not physically reachable. Evaluation all 7*256 even unreachable. Need rules satisfy policy for all, not infer relationships between Boolean inputs beyond one-hot mode flags. We must not rely on physical reachability, only mode flags one-hot. Our rules don't rely on relationships except one-hot? We use ModeBrakeRequested and ModeStopped. Fine.\n\nBut need be careful: Policy says \"For each step, apply the first applicable requirement below. Later requirements never override an earlier requirement, irrespective of current mode.\" Our ordering should exactly map requirements. Let's test all combinations logically.\n\nLet B = unusable/inactive/blocked.\n\nOrder:\n1 B and Halted -> Brake/Stopped.\n2 B and not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested.\n3 AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish/Done.\n4 AtGoal and Released and not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested.\n5 OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ -> Release/Traversing.\n6 ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted -> Brake/BrakeRequested.\n7 not OwnReservation and not Released -> Request/Waiting.\n8 ModeStopped -> Resume/ResumePending.\n9 True -> Proceed/Traversing.\n\nCompare policy:\n1 if B. Our rules 1/2 handle B. Good.\n2 else if not B and AtGoal and Released. Our rules 3/4 handle AtGoal Released regardless B, but B already handled. If not B, rule3/4. Good. If B, earlier. Good.\n3 else if (not B and not (AtGoal&Released)? Actually after previous) and OwnReservation and BodyClear. Our rule5 handles OwnReservation BodyClear after B and AtGoalReleased. Since B and AtGoalReleased earlier. If B true, earlier. If AtGoal&Released true, earlier. If neither, rule5. Good. Condition \"neither previous applies\" includes not B and not(AtGoal&Released). Rule5 might apply when B true? earlier. When AtGoalReleased true? earlier. So after order, only applies when neither. Good.\n4 else if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted. Our rule6 after rule5. If earlier applies, earlier. If no earlier, and mode BrakeRequested not Halted. Good. But what if B false, AtGoalReleased false, OwnReservation BodyClear false, ModeBrakeRequested not Halted. Rule6. Good.\n5 else if not OwnReservation and not Released. Our rule7 after rule6. If earlier applies, earlier. If no earlier, and both false. Good.\n6 else if ModeStopped. Our rule8 after rule7. If no earlier, and mode stopped. Good.\n7 else Proceed. Good.\n\nNeed check if rule5 OwnReservation BodyClear can override rule4 ModeBrakeRequested? Policy req3 before req4. Yes. Our rule5 before rule6. Good.\nWhat about rule5 OwnReservation BodyClear and Halted? No condition on Halted. If ModeBrakeRequested Halted false, Release. Correct req3 priority.\nWhat about rule5 OwnReservation BodyClear and mode Stopped? Req3 before req6, so Release/Traversing, not Resume. Our rule5 before rule8. Correct. Policy req3 \"This takes priority even if current mode is BrakeRequested.\" But not limited. It is req3 before req4 etc. So yes.\nWhat about rule5 OwnReservation BodyClear and both OwnReservation and Released? If Released true, condition not both false. But rule5 anyway. If OwnReservation true and BodyClear true, Released could true. Req3 applies if neither previous and OwnReservation/BodyClear. It doesn't care Released. But if AtGoal and Released true, req2 earlier. If not AtGoal, Released may true. Req3 still applies? Let's read: \"If neither of the previous requirements applies and OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ are true, return Release...\" Previous req2 requires AtGoal and Released. If Released true but AtGoal false, req2 not apply. So req3 applies. Our rule5. Good.\nWhat if Released true, AtGoal false, OwnReservation true, BodyClear true, ModeBrakeRequested Halted false. Req3 before req4, Release. Our rule5. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Requirement 2 says \"With those blocking conditions absent, a robot that is AtGoal and has Released...\" If B false. Our rule3/4 don't check B, but B earlier. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Requirement 3 says \"If neither previous applies and OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ are true...\" The word \"neither previous\" means neither req1 nor req2 applies. We rely on ordering. Good.\n\nPotential issue: Requirement 5 says \"Otherwise, if both OwnReservation and Released are false...\" This is after req4. Our rule7 after rule6. But what if ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted and both false? Req4 applies before req5, so Brake/BrakeRequested. Our rule6 before rule7. Good.\nWhat if ModeBrakeRequested and Halted true and both false? Req4 false (Halted false required). Req5 applies. Our rule6 false because not Halted false; rule7 true. Good. Policy: req4 otherwise ... in BrakeRequested with Halted false. If Halted true, skip to req5. Yes.\n\nWhat if ModeStopped and both false and Halted false? Req5 applies before req6, so Request/Waiting. Our rule7 before rule8. Good. Even though mode stopped, if both OwnReservation and Released false, request. Policy req5 before req6. Yes.\n\nWhat if ModeStopped and OwnReservation true or Released true. Req5 false. Req6 applies. Our rule8. Good.\n\nWhat if ModeStopped, Released false, OwnReservation false, Halted false? Req5 true -> Request/Waiting. Our rule7. Good.\n\nWhat if ModeDone and no earlier conditions. Rule9 Proceed/Traversing. Policy req7 remaining. It says no terminal-mode shortcut, requirements apply in every mode including Done. So Done can Proceed? According to remaining case, yes. That seems odd but specified. Our final true. Good.\n\nNeed ensure mode names in `next` are exactly one of Idle, Waiting, Traversing, BrakeRequested, Stopped, ResumePending, Done. We use Stopped, BrakeRequested, Done, Traversing, Waiting, ResumePending. No Idle used. That's okay. Need action strings exact: Request, Proceed, Brake, Resume, Release, Finish. We use.\n\nNeed schema root exactly three keys: \"schema\", \"select\", \"step\". We need ensure no extra fields. Each select rule exactly \"when\" and \"action\". Each step rule exactly \"when\", \"action\", \"next\". JSON object. Need no trailing commas. Need UTF-8. Good.\n\nNow, check constraints: \"At most 32 total branches are allowed; the per-function limit of twelve still applies.\" We have 4+9=13. \"branch\" maybe number of rules? If branch means conditions? Anyway <=32. Per function <=12 yes.\n\n\"Source size at most 200 * 1024 bytes.\" Our JSON small.\n\n\"Duplicate JSON keys rejected.\" We have unique keys per object. Root unique. Good.\n\n\"Every possible input must have a result.\" Select final True. Step final True. Good.\n\n\"Expressions allow only True, False, permitted Boolean names, not, and, or, and parentheses, with Python Boolean precedence. No calls, comparisons, arithmetic, attributes, new names, or assignment.\" Our expressions use only names and operators. Need ensure no `!`, no `!=`. Good.\n\n\"select cannot use any step or mode names; step cannot use any select names.\" Our select uses OwnerFree, RequestA, RequestB, Prefer? Actually we don't use Prefer. That's allowed. Step uses step facts and mode flags, not select names. Good.\n\nNeed maybe consider if step can use `Halted` and mode flags. Yes.\n\nNow, let's think if there is any hidden issue with \"When both robots are eligible, either is legal; preferences do not impose an additional acceptance obligation, and their values may conflict or both be absent.\" Our select rule3 picks A when both eligible even if PreferB true. Is that legal? It says either is legal, preferences advisory no obligation. Yes. But if there is a preference, could they expect use? No, not required. The policy \"select an eligible robot, rather than Defer\" only. So any eligible. Our rule3 picks A. Good.\n\nPotential issue: \"Selecting A requires OwnerFree and RequestA; selecting B requires OwnerFree and RequestB.\" Our rule3 when both true selects A. Good. Rule1 selects A when RequestA true, RequestB false. Rule2 selects B when RequestB true, RequestA false. Good.\n\nPotential issue: If OwnerFree true, RequestA true, RequestB false, PreferB true, our rule1 SelectA. Is that allowed? RequestB false, B not eligible. So must select A. Preferences don't matter. Good.\n\nNow, let's ensure expressions have correct Python syntax. For rule1 select: `\"OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB\"`. Python precedence: `not` before `and`, so `(OwnerFree and RequestA and (not RequestB))`. Good.\nRule2: `\"OwnerFree and RequestB and not RequestA\"`. Good.\nRule3: `\"OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB\"`. Good.\nRule4: `\"True\"`. Good.\n\nStep rule1: `\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\"`\nPython: inside parentheses: `((not ObservationUsable) or (not TaskActive) or PedestrianBlocked)`. Then and Halted. Good.\nRule2: `\"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\"`. Python: `(B) and (not Halted)`. Good.\nRule3: `\"AtGoal and Released and Halted\"`.\nRule4: `\"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\"`. Good.\nRule5: `\"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\"`.\nRule6: `\"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\"`.\nRule7: `\"not OwnReservation and not Released\"`. Python: `(not OwnReservation) and (not Released)`. Good.\nRule8: `\"ModeStopped\"`.\nRule9: `\"True\"`.\n\nNeed consider AST depth <=8 for expressions. All small. Rule1 depth maybe 4. Good. Condition length <=512. Good.\n\nNow, final answer must be exactly one UTF-8 JSON object, no Markdown. We'll output compact or pretty? They said no Markdown fences, explanatory prose. JSON can be pretty. Need ensure exactly one JSON object. Pretty with newlines is okay. But maybe to be safe, compact. No additional fields. We'll output minified? Could output pretty. The final answer should be only JSON. I'll output compact single line or pretty. Since desired oververbosity 5 but task demands exact JSON. I'll output compact but readable. Need ensure no trailing commas. Let's construct:\n\n{\n  \"schema\": \"amr-supervisor/v1\",\n  \"select\": [\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA and not RequestB\", \"action\": \"SelectA\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestB and not RequestA\", \"action\": \"SelectB\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnerFree and RequestA and RequestB\", \"action\": \"SelectA\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Defer\"}\n  ],\n  \"step\": [\n    {\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"Stopped\"},\n    {\"when\": \"(not ObservationUsable or not TaskActive or PedestrianBlocked) and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and Halted\", \"action\": \"Finish\", \"next\": \"Done\"},\n    {\"when\": \"AtGoal and Released and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"OwnReservation and BodyClearOfZ\", \"action\": \"Release\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeBrakeRequested and not Halted\", \"action\": \"Brake\", \"next\": \"BrakeRequested\"},\n    {\"when\": \"not OwnReservation and not Released\", \"action\": \"Request\", \"next\": \"Waiting\"},\n    {\"when\": \"ModeStopped\", \"action\": \"Resume\", \"next\": \"ResumePending\"},\n    {\"when\": \"True\", \"action\": \"Proceed\", \"next\": \"Traversing\"}\n  ]\n}\n\nCheck step rule3: AtGoal and Released and Halted -> Finish Done. But wait policy r